.\" SlimStack Manual Page
.\" Generated for SlimStack v0.1.0
.TH SLIM 1 "January 2025" "SlimStack 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slim \- dependency hygiene and waste elimination CLI tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slim
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B SlimStack
is a CLI tool that helps developers identify, visualize, and safely remove unused dependencies and dependency bloat across Python and Node.js projects.
.PP
It analyzes your codebase using static analysis (AST for Python, regex for JavaScript/TypeScript) to determine which installed packages are actually being used.
.PP
.B Key features:
.IP \(bu 2
Python dependency analysis using AST-based import detection
.IP \(bu 2
Node.js dependency analysis with require/import detection
.IP \(bu 2
Disk usage visualization with ASCII charts
.IP \(bu 2
Safe pruning with dry-run default and confirmation prompts
.IP \(bu 2
JSON output for CI/CD integration
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "General Commands"
.TP
.B slim version
Display the current version of SlimStack.
.TP
.B slim help
Display usage help and examples.
.SS "Python Commands"
.TP
.B slim py scan
Scan the current Python project for dependencies. Detects which installed packages are used, unused, or transitive-only.
.TP
.B slim py scan \-\-json
Output scan results as JSON for machine processing.
.TP
.B slim py scan \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Scan a specific project path instead of current directory.
.TP
.B slim py prune
Show unused packages that can be removed (dry-run mode, no changes made).
.TP
.B slim py prune \-\-force
Actually remove unused packages. Will prompt for confirmation before deletion.
.TP
.B slim py prune \-\-json
Output prune results as JSON.
.SS "Node.js Commands"
.TP
.B slim node scan
Scan the current Node.js project for dependencies. Reads package.json and compares against actual imports in source files.
.TP
.B slim node scan \-\-json
Output scan results as JSON.
.TP
.B slim node scan \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Scan a specific project path instead of current directory.
.TP
.B slim node prune
Show unused packages that can be removed (dry-run mode).
.TP
.B slim node prune \-\-force
Actually remove unused packages using npm uninstall.
.TP
.B slim node prune \-\-include\-dev
Also include unused devDependencies in the prune list.
.SS "Disk Usage Commands"
.TP
.B slim disk
Show disk usage by ecosystem (Python, Node.js, Docker).
.TP
.B slim disk \-\-by project
Group disk usage by project instead of ecosystem.
.TP
.B slim disk \-\-top \fIN\fR
Limit results to top N items by size.
.TP
.B slim disk \-\-path \fIPATH\fR
Scan a specific directory instead of current directory.
.TP
.B slim disk \-\-json
Output disk usage as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results in JSON format for machine processing. Available on all scan and prune commands.
.TP
.B \-\-path, \-p \fIPATH\fR
Specify project path. Defaults to current working directory.
.TP
.B \-\-force
For prune commands: actually remove packages (with confirmation prompt). Without this flag, prune runs in dry-run mode.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
For prune commands: show what would be removed without making changes. This is the default behavior.
.TP
.B \-\-top \fIN\fR
For disk command: limit number of results displayed.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-dev
For node prune: include devDependencies in the removal list.
.SH SAFETY
.B SlimStack
is designed with safety as a priority:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRead-only by default\fR: All scan commands never modify anything.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDry-run default\fR: Prune commands show what would be removed without actually removing anything.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBConfirmation prompts\fR: The \-\-force flag requires explicit "y" confirmation before deletion.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBVirtual environment protection\fR: Python pruning requires running inside a virtual environment.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBProtected packages\fR: pip, setuptools, and wheel are never removed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan a Python project:
.RS
.nf
$ slim py scan
.fi
.RE
.PP
Get JSON output for CI/CD:
.RS
.nf
$ slim py scan --json > deps.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview unused packages:
.RS
.nf
$ slim py prune
.fi
.RE
.PP
Remove unused packages:
.RS
.nf
$ slim py prune --force
.fi
.RE
.PP
Check disk usage:
.RS
.nf
$ slim disk --top 10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Scan a specific path:
.RS
.nf
$ slim py scan --path /path/to/project
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (missing package.json, not in virtualenv for prune, etc.)
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by user (Ctrl+C)
.SH FILES
.TP
.I pyproject.toml, setup.py
Python project markers
.TP
.I package.json
Node.js project marker
.TP
.I venv/, .venv/, env/
Python virtual environment directories
.TP
.I node_modules/
Node.js dependencies directory
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIRTUAL_ENV
If set, indicates an active Python virtual environment.
.SH BUGS
Dynamic imports (e.g., \fB__import__(name)\fR in Python or \fBrequire(variable)\fR in Node.js) cannot be detected by static analysis and are logged as "unknown".
.PP
Report bugs at: https://github.com/arceuzvx/SlimStack/issues
